    "body":  "## Summary\n\nAdds a Sentry connector to Switch using Sentry\u0027s official remote MCP server and OAuth authentication.\n\nThe integration allows the Switch connector architecture to expose Sentry\u0027s diagnostic tools to authorised agents, with verified account identity handling, credential boundaries, and agent safety instructions.\n\nRelated to #820.\n\n## Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"Switch Console\"] --\u003e B[\"Sentry OAuth Connection\"]\n    B --\u003e C[\"OAuth Registration and PKCE\"]\n    C --\u003e D[\"Sentry Authorization\"]\n    D --\u003e E[\"MCP Identity Verification\"]\n    E --\u003e F[\"Switch Connection\"]\n    F --\u003e G[\"Agent Grant\"]\n    G --\u003e H[\"Session Host MCP Proxy\"]\n    H --\u003e I[\"Sentry Remote MCP Server\"]\n    I --\u003e J[\"Issues, Events, Stack Traces, Releases\"]\n```\n\n## Implementation\n\n* Added an enabled Sentry connector catalog entry.\n* Integrated the official remote MCP endpoint at `https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp`.\n* Implemented OAuth dynamic registration and structured MCP identity verification.\n* Used the required `tools: { mode: pass_through }` configuration.\n* Configured an honestly described write-capable access level rather than claiming unverified read-only restrictions.\n* Added reusable MCP identity handling and related OAuth, loader, registry, and flow changes.\n* Added the Sentry investigation skill for issues, events, stack traces, and releases.\n* Added the official Sentry SVG, attribution, and Console integration.\n* Added tests for authentication, catalog configuration, identity validation, and security boundaries.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Focused Sentry tests | 33 passed |\n| Broader Core tests | 485 passed; one lifecycle fixture initially failed |\n| Corrected lifecycle fixture | Passed in focused rerun |\n| Python lint and formatting | Passed |\n| Mypy | Passed |\n| Console builds and typechecks | Passed |\n| Console logo tests | 38 passed |\n| Agent-provider tests | 946 passed, 8 skipped |\n| Live OAuth metadata discovery | Passed |\n\nThe full broader Core suite was not reported as rerun after the lifecycle fixture correction.\n\n## Security\n\n* Enforces HTTPS, PKCE, strict identity validation, and bounded responses.\n* Rejects unexpected redirects during identity verification.\n* Sanitises authentication errors.\n* Preserves existing token-lifetime limits.\n* Provides safety guidance for sensitive diagnostics and destructive operations.\n\n## Known limitation: OAuth refresh\n\nSentry\u0027s current OAuth refresh behaviour may produce tokens whose lifetime exceeds Switch\u0027s enforced lifetime cap.\n\nSwitch continues rejecting tokens outside its accepted lifetime policy. Automatic refresh therefore requires additional live verification and may need a separately reviewed compatibility solution.\n\n## Outstanding acceptance criteria\n\n* Credentialed Sentry sign-in.\n* Real agent MCP tool execution from a room.\n* Successful token renewal.\n* Grant removal and disconnect behaviour.\n* Transcript/log credential-disclosure checks.\n* Requested end-to-end demonstration video.\n\n## Commit\n\n`f53b588b`\n\nThis PR includes the implementation and local validation, but should remain a draft until the refresh-compatibility risk and live acceptance requirements are addressed.",
